  partName: Bolt (9)
  description: The Bolt (9) is a tiny, complex fastener situated at the top-center-front
    of the engine, responsible for securing various engine components such as the
    cylinder head, engine block, and other critical parts. Made of Material.001,
    this bolt provides a strong and reliable connection, ensuring the engine's structural
    integrity and performance. One interesting aspect of this bolt is its ability
    to be used in a variety of torque settings, allowing for precise control over
    the engine's assembly and operation.
